{
  "_readme": "Maps each CM5 native-MQTT-Publisher topic to the ordered list of tag names carried in that topic's payload. Keyed on the FULL topic string, deliberately -- two panels are in play and both use gN suffixes, so matching on the suffix alone would let one overwrite the other. UPDATED 2026-08-07 (fourth revision) to add the Lab bench on its own namespace. TRUCK (RAIV-2), raiv-tracker/truck-2/hmi/g1..g73: 73 topics in Publisher objects of exactly 10 -- P1=g1..g10, P2=g11..g20, P3=g21..g30, P4=g31..g40, P5=g41..g50 (those five fill broker connection 1, which caps at 50 topics), then P6=g51..g60, P7=g61..g70, P8=g71..g73 on a SECOND broker connection. g41..g73 are the 33 tags migrated off StrideLinx so its Modbus polling could leave the machine network; note RejectPartsCount is not among them because it is already g20. LAB BENCH, raiv-tracker/lab/hmi/g1..g40: the bench runs a near-identical program, so it carries the same 40 tags as the truck's Publishers 1-4 but publishes on its own prefix. It was moved off the truck's namespace on 2026-08-07 after it was found publishing into raiv-tracker/truck-2/* and being logged as truck data; anything logged under truck-2 between roughly 17:36 and 20:0x UTC that day is bench data, not the truck. Bench values are mostly zero -- it has no stored production data. Every row is PayloadType=1 (raw tag value), so each list below has exactly one entry; the parser splits on '|' and zips positionally, so it handles one value or several without code changes. This file and the TAG_BY_GROUP table inside cm5.html must be kept in sync for the truck topics.",
